{"abstract":"Reinforcement learning (RL) has shown promise in solving various combinatorial optimization problems. However, conventional RL faces challenges when dealing with real-world constraints, especially when action space feasibility is explicit and dependent on the corresponding state or trajectory. In this work, we focus on using RL in container shipping, often considered the cornerstone of global trade, by dealing with the critical challenge of master stowage planning. The main objective is to maximize cargo revenue and minimize operational costs while navigating demand uncertainty and various complex operational constraints, namely vessel capacity and stability, which must be dynamically updated along the vessel's voyage. To address this problem, we implement a deep reinforcement learning framework with feasibility projection to solve the master stowage planning problem (MPP) under demand uncertainty. The experimental results show that our architecture efficiently finds adaptive, feasible solutions for this multi-stage stochastic optimization problem, outperforming traditional mixed-integer programming and RL with feasibility regularization. Our AI-driven decision-support policy enables adaptive and feasible planning under uncertainty, optimizing operational efficiency and capacity utilization while contributing to sustainable and resilient global supply chains.","author_count":5,"contributors":["van Twiller, Jaike","Adulyasak, Yossiri","Delage, Erick","Grbic, Djordje","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828163"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","HEC Montréal"],"keyword":["Combinatorial optimization","Machine learning","Maritime logistics","Reinforcement learning","Stochastic optimization","Transportation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"navigating demand uncertainty in container shipping deep reinforcement learning for enabling adaptive and feasible master stowage planning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2502.12756","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-828163","ids":["itu-85b71ca7-6f77-4d8b-9650-0ae57a5df79c"],"keyword":["Combinatorial optimization","Feasibility projection","Machine learning","Maritime logistics","Reinforcement learning","Transportation","stochastic optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C72F9DFF8386788C53E6658CC215FE1C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2502.12756","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"hec montréal","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"HEC Montréal","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaike","key":"vantwillerpau","last":"van Twiller","locid":"fa03d816-cd99-4fea-b45b-efe7ecd3cb0a","name":"van Twiller, Jaike","orcid":"0000-0001-8390-1629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yossiri","key":"adulyasakpau","last":"Adulyasak","name":"Adulyasak, Yossiri","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erick","key":"delagepau","last":"Delage","name":"Delage, Erick","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-85b71ca7-6f77-4d8b-9650-0ae57a5df79c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Navigating Demand Uncertainty in Container Shipping: Deep Reinforcement Learning for Enabling Adaptive and Feasible Master Stowage Planning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828163","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["van Twiller, Jaike","Grbic, Djordje","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798526"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Container stowage planning","Deep reinforcement learning","Maritime logistics","Markov decision process"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep reinforcement learning for master stowage planning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108728660/abstracts.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798526","ids":["itu-322d98a1-2942-418b-9da9-45b6752dd133"],"keyword":["Container stowage planning","Deep reinforcement learning","Maritime logistics","Markov decision process"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D6B9792D555D40679E91177ACA0A97BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108728660/abstracts.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, The Maritime Hub"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaike","key":"vantwillerpau","last":"van Twiller","locid":"fa03d816-cd99-4fea-b45b-efe7ecd3cb0a","name":"van Twiller, Jaike","orcid":"0000-0001-8390-1629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"9th","place":"Carmona, Spain","status":"p","subtitle":"International Workshop on Freight Transportation and Logistics","title":"ODYSSEUS 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-322d98a1-2942-418b-9da9-45b6752dd133"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep Reinforcement Learning for Master Stowage Planning","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798526","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Efficient supply chains are vital for both the worldwide economy and environmental sustainability. Container shipping plays a key role in this, known for being an eco-friendly mode of transport. Liner shipping companies are actively working to improve operational efficiency through stowage planning. Due to many combinatorial aspects, some of which are NP-hard, stowage planning is a challenging problem in its representative form. Even though stowage planning can be decomposed into master and slot planning, the subproblems remain challenging. As a result, we are searching for scalable algorithms to solve the stowage planning problem. In this work, we propose Proximal Policy optimization for master STOWage planning (PPSTOW), a deep reinforcement learning approach to address master planning with focus on global problem objectives and constraints. The experiments show the effectiveness of PPSTOW, as the framework efficiently finds near-optimal solutions for simulated problem instances with realistic vessel sizes and practical planning horizons. In the future, we aim to refine the representativeness of our approach by integrating revenue management, as well as local problem objectives and constraints.","author_count":3,"contributors":["van Twiller, Jaike","Grbic, Djordje","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818250"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Combinatorial optimization","Deep reinforcement learning","Maritime logistics","Stowage planning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ppstow an end to end deep reinforcement learning model for master stowage planning on container vessels","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109457848/Euro2024_Copenhagen_Program.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818250","ids":["itu-abf6eac6-433a-479e-96d5-e136dd18bc61"],"keyword":["Combinatorial Optimization","Deep reinforcement learning","Maritime logistics","Stowage planning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-424E4E8B90748CF39F9FC9E4A2E1B6D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109457848/Euro2024_Copenhagen_Program.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaike","key":"vantwillerpau","last":"van Twiller","locid":"fa03d816-cd99-4fea-b45b-efe7ecd3cb0a","name":"van Twiller, Jaike","orcid":"0000-0001-8390-1629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-abf6eac6-433a-479e-96d5-e136dd18bc61"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"PPSTOW: An End-to-End Deep Reinforcement Learning Model for Master Stowage Planning on Container Vessels","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818250","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This short paper focuses on procedurally generating rules and communicating them to players to adjust the difficulty. This is part of a larger project to collect and adapt games in educational games for young children using a digital puzzle game designed for kindergartens. A genetic algorithm is used together with a difficulty measure to find a target number of solution sets and a large language model is used to communicate the rules in a narrative context. During testing the approach was able to find rules that approximate any given target difficulty within two dozen generations on average. The approach was combined with a large language model to create a narrative puzzle game where players have to host a dinner for animals that can't get along. Future experiments will try to improve evaluation, specialize the language model on children's literature, and collect multi-modal data from players to guide adaptation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Volden, Thomas Vase Schultz","Grbic, Djordje","Burelli, Paolo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718832"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Difficulty adjustment","Educational games","Genetic algorithm","Large Language Models","Procedural Generation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"procedurally generating rules to adapt difficulty for narrative puzzle games","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2307.05518","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718832","identifier":[{"id":"85180554237","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1a158d41-175f-41ff-a1b9-08edad2f7bcd"],"keyword":["difficulty adjustment","educational games","genetic algorithm","large language models","procedural generation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-B34EC7EEDC9D83C5801381727E6815BF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100051811/IEEE_COG_2023_Yoli_Short.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2307.05518","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"voldenpau","last":"Volden","locid":"7e884581-3d40-42e6-af12-453e052c9c87","name":"Volden, Thomas Vase Schultz","name_org":"Volden, Thomas","orcid":"0009-0009-2177-5482","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"burellipau","last":"Burelli","locid":"cf5e1d64-5489-4534-ba34-8dba5fd354a6","name":"Burelli, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0003-2804-9028","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2307.05518","eisbn":["9798350322774"],"isbn":["9798350322781"],"pages":"1-4","publisher":"IEEE","series":"Proceedings of the 2023 IEEE conference on Games","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the IEEE Conference on Game"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85180554237"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1a158d41-175f-41ff-a1b9-08edad2f7bcd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Procedurally generating rules to adapt difficulty for narrative puzzle games","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718832","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Major liner shipping companies aim to solve the stowage planning problem by optimally allocating containers to vessel locations during a multi-port voyage. Due to a large variety of combinatorial aspects, a scalable algorithm to solve a representative problem is yet to be found. This paper will show that deep reinforcement learning can optimize a non-trivial master bay planning problem. Our experiments show that proximal policy optimization efficiently finds reasonable solutions, serving as preliminary evidence of the potential value of deep reinforcement learning in stowage planning. In future work, we will extend our architecture to address a full-featured master bay planning problem.","author_count":7,"contributors":["van Twiller, Jaike","Grbic, Djordje","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695235"],"event":{"acronym":"ICCL","title":"International Conference on Computational Logistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deep reinforcement learning","Liner shipping","Maritime logistics","Markov decision processes","Stowage planning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a deep reinforcement learning model of master bay stowage planning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108495311/978-3-031-43612-3_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695235","identifier":[{"id":"85172314690","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3f8da0cf-0e96-4f0d-a428-2e9d50067227"],"keyword":["Deep reinforcement learning","Liner shipping","Maritime logistics","Markov decision processes","Stowage planning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B86C238147910466D3061DC40DA7996"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108495311/978-3-031-43612-3_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaike","key":"vantwillerpau","last":"van Twiller","locid":"fa03d816-cd99-4fea-b45b-efe7ecd3cb0a","name":"van Twiller, Jaike","orcid":"0000-0001-8390-1629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J.R.","key":"dadunapedh","last":"Daduna","name":"Daduna, J.R.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"G.","key":"liedtkepedh","last":"Liedtke","name":"Liedtke, G.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"X.","key":"shipedh","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, X.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"S.","key":"voßpedh","last":"Voß","name":"Voß, S.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-43612-3_6","eisbn":["9783031436123"],"isbn":["9783031436116"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"105-121","place":"Berlin","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"ICCL 2023: Computational Logistics","volume":"14239"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172314690"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3f8da0cf-0e96-4f0d-a428-2e9d50067227"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards a Deep Reinforcement Learning Model of Master Bay Stowage Planning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695235","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background Simulating DNA evolution has been done through coevolution-agnostic probabilistic frameworks for the past 3 decades. The most common implementation is by using the converse of the probabilistic approach used to infer phylogenies which, in the simplest form, simulates a single sequence at a time. However, biological systems are multi-genic, and gene products can affect each other’s evolutionary paths through coevolution. These crucial evolutionary dynamics still remain to be simulated, and we believe that modelling them can lead to profound insights for comparative genomics. Results Here we present CastNet, a genome evolution simulator that assumes each genome is a collection of genes with constantly evolving regulatory interactions in between them. The regulatory interactions produce a phenotype in the form of gene expression profiles, upon which fitness is calculated. A genetic algorithm is then used to evolve a population of such entities through a user-defined phylogeny. Importantly, the regulatory mutations are a response to sequence mutations, thus making a 1–1 relationship between the rate of evolution of sequences and of regulatory parameters. This is, to our knowledge, the first time the evolution of sequences and regulation have been explicitly linked in a simulation, despite there being a multitude of sequence evolution simulators, and a handful of models to simulate Gene Regulatory Network (GRN) evolution. In our test runs, we see a coevolutionary signal among genes that are active in the GRN, and neutral evolution in genes that are not included in the network, showing that selective pressures imposed on the regulatory output of the genes are reflected in their sequences. Conclusion We believe that CastNet represents a substantial step for developing new tools to study genome evolution, and more broadly, coevolutionary webs and complex evolving systems. This simulator also provides a new framework to study molecular evolution where sequence coevolution has a leading role.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Rivera-Rivera, Carlos J.","Grbic, Djordje"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718819"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bristol"],"keyword":["Coevolution","Coevolutionary webs","Complex systems","Evo devo","Evolution simulation","Evolutionary systems","Gene Regulatory Networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"castnet a systems level sequence evolution simulator","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102802886/s12859-023-05366-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718819","identifier":[{"id":"85161878247","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-005e3f5f-7bef-4955-97a4-ce900a8b1bd5"],"keyword":["Coevolution","Coevolutionary webs","Complex systems","Evo-devo","Evolution simulation","Evolutionary systems","Gene regulatory networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4630AE0A14C15AE86FBB6E31B86EDAF5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://bmcbioinformatics.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s12859-023-05366-1","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102802886/s12859-023-05366-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of bristol","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bristol","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlos J.","key":"riverariverapau","last":"Rivera-Rivera","name":"Rivera-Rivera, Carlos J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-005e3f5f-7bef-4955-97a4-ce900a8b1bd5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CastNet: a systems-level sequence evolution simulator","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718819","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces EvoCraft, a framework for Minecraft designed to study open-ended algorithms. We introduce an API that provides an open-source Python interface for communicating with Minecraft to place and track blocks. In contrast to previous work in Minecraft that focused on learning to play the game, the grand challenge we pose here is to automatically search for increasingly complex artifacts in an open-ended fashion. Compared to other environments used to study open-endedness, Minecraft allows the construction of almost any kind of structure, including actuated machines with circuits and mechanical components. We present initial baseline results in evolving simple Minecraft creations through both interactive and automated evolution. While evolution succeeds when tasked to grow a structure towards a specific target, it is unable to find a solution when rewarded for creating a simple machine that moves. Thus, EvoCraft offers a challenging new environment for automated search methods (such as evolution) to find complex artifacts that we hope will spur the development of more open-ended algorithms. A Python implementation of the EvoCraft framework is available at: github.com/real-itu/Evocraft-py.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Berg Palm, Rasmus","Najarro, Elias","Glanois, Claire","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382906"],"event":{"acronym":"EvoApplications","title":"European Conference on the Applications of Evolutionary Computation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary computation","MIECRAFT","Open ended evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evocraft a new challenge for open endedness","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421848/2012.04751.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382906","ids":["itu-6e406c79-2b12-4d2d-a7ab-a2aa0aedef80"],"keyword":["Evolutionary computation","MIECRAFT","OPEN ENDED EVOLUTION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B3563055C60A4A0D2D68E0538909CC59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421848/2012.04751.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"bergpalmpau","last":"Berg Palm","name":"Berg Palm, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"Applications of Evolutionary Computation","status":"p","title":"Applications of Evolutionary Computation","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6e406c79-2b12-4d2d-a7ab-a2aa0aedef80"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EvoCraft: A New Challenge for Open-Endedness","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382906","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Neural Cellular Automata (NCAs) have been proven effective in simulating morphogenetic processes, the continuous construction of complex structures from very few starting cells. Recent developments in NCAs lie in the 2D domain, namely reconstructing target images from a single pixel or infinitely growing 2D textures. In this work, we propose an extension of NCAs to 3D, utilizing 3D convolutions in the proposed neural network architecture. Minecraft is selected as the environment for our automaton since it allows the generation of both static structures and moving machines. We show that despite their simplicity, NCAs are capable of growing complex entities such as castles, apartment blocks, and trees, some of which are composed of over 3,000 blocks. Additionally, when trained for regeneration, the system is able to regrow parts of simple functional machines, significantly expanding the capabilities of simulated morphogenetic systems. The code for the experiment in this paper can be found at: https://github.com/real-itu/3d-artefacts-nca.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sudhakaran, Shyam","Grbic, Djordje","Li, Siyan","Katona, Adam","Najarro, Elias","Glanois, Claire","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383561"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cellular automata","Minecraft","Neural Cellular Automata","Open ended evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"growing 000000000003d artefacts and functional machines with neural cellular automata","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421939/isal_a_00451.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383561","identifier":[{"id":"86000272077","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9cfbe7f0-0225-46d0-ac0e-eaca10caa909"],"keyword":["Minecraft","Neural Cellular Automata","cellular automata","open ended evolution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F452FA7C08B2A4307CD75B7EBE9D26C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421939/isal_a_00451.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shyam","key":"sudhakaranpau","last":"Sudhakaran","locid":"b4a6e67f-0caa-4faf-a136-bf77496f3659","name":"Sudhakaran, Shyam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Siyan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"71efb6df-0032-4f63-9a05-8489aedd9023","name":"Li, Siyan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Adam","key":"katonapau","last":"Katona","name":"Katona, Adam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["26931508"],"journal":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","volume":"2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000272077"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9cfbe7f0-0225-46d0-ac0e-eaca10caa909"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Growing 3D Artefacts and Functional Machines with Neural Cellular Automata","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383561","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Random exploration is one of the main mechanisms through which reinforcement learning (RL) finds well-performing policies. However, it can lead to undesirable or catastrophic outcomes when learning online in safety-critical environments. In fact, safe learning is one of the major obstacles towards real-world agents that can learn during deployment. One way of ensuring that agents respect hard limitations is to explicitly configure boundaries in which they can operate. While this might work in some cases, we do not always have clear a-priori information which states and actions can lead dangerously close to hazardous states. Here, we present an approach where an additional policy can override the main policy and offer a safer alternative action. In our instinct-regulated RL (IR2L) approach, an “instinctual” network is trained to recognize undesirable situations, while guarding the learning policy against entering them. The instinct network is pre-trained on a single task where it is safe to make mistakes, and transferred to environments in which learning a new task safely is critical. We demonstrate IR2L in the OpenAI Safety gym domain, in which it receives a significantly lower number of safety violations during training than a baseline RL approach while reaching similar task performance.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381718"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Life long learning","Reinforcement learning","Safe reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safer reinforcement learning through transferable instinct networks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86422010/isal_a_00449.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381718","identifier":[{"id":"86000265479","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1e472bea-7f01-4e7a-a4ab-b9ac2c193e86"],"keyword":["Life-long learning","Reinforcement learning","safe reinforcement learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F89D1E98E7D256336E700FC19E45C698"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86422010/isal_a_00449.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["26931508"],"issue":"2021","journal":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000265479"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1e472bea-7f01-4e7a-a4ab-b9ac2c193e86"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Safer Reinforcement Learning through Transferable Instinct Networks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381718","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"An important goal in reinforcement learning is to create agents that can quickly adapt to new goals but at the same time avoid situations that might cause damage to themselves or their environments. One way agents learn is through exploration mechanisms, which are needed to discover new policies. However, in deep reinforcement learning, exploration is normally done by injecting noise in the action space. While performing well in many domains, this setup has the inherent risk that the noisy actions lead agents to unsafe environment states. In this paper, we introduce a novel approach called Meta-Learned Instinctual Networks (MLIN) that allows agents to perform lifetime learning while avoiding hazardous states. At the core of the approach is a plastic network trained through reinforcement learning and an evolved \"instinctual\" network, which does not change during the agent's lifetime but can modulate the noisy output of the plastic network. We test our idea on a simple 2D navigation task with hazard zones, in which the agent has to learn to approach new targets during deployment. While a standard meta-trained network performs poorly in these tasks, MLIN allows agents to learn to navigate to new targets while minimizing collisions with hazard zones. These results suggest that meta-learning augmented with an instinctual network is a promising approach for safe AI.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382937"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary algorithms","Life long learning","Reinforcement learning","Safe reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safer reinforcement learning through evolved instincts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85571059/GECCO_2020_Grbic_Risi_POSTER.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382937","identifier":[{"id":"85089735740","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-704b619d-f68e-4cf8-824d-39507d649551"],"keyword":["Evolutionary algorithms","Life-long learning","Reinforcement learning","safe reinforcement learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-10A42B9ABCF563F3F4F9E053D00AA3F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85571059/GECCO_2020_Grbic_Risi_POSTER.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3377929.3389946","isbn":["9781450371278"],"pages":"77-78","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2020 Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion","title":"GECCO '20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089735740"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-704b619d-f68e-4cf8-824d-39507d649551"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Safer reinforcement learning through evolved instincts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382937","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This work investigates the evolution of indirectly-encoded neural networks through a hypernetwork approach. We find that for some Atari games, a hypernetwork with over 14 times fewer parameters, can compete or even outperform directly-encoded policy networks. While hypernetworks perform worse than directly encoded networks in the game Frostbite, in the game Gravitar, the approach reaches a higher score than any other evolutionary method and outperforms complicated deep reinforcement learning setups such as Rainbow.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Carvelli, Christain","Grbic, Djordje","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381315"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Evolutionary algorithms","Game playing agents","Hypernetworks","Machine learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving hypernetworks for game playing agents","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85571064/crvelli_grbic_risi_2020.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381315","identifier":[{"id":"85089726267","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-03c46043-9784-4720-a144-78e3a6855258"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Evolutionary algorithms","Game-playing agents","Hypernetworks","Machine learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5827ECD8253F4A8E6684634DEB361682"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85571064/crvelli_grbic_risi_2020.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["modl.ai"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christain","key":"carvellipau","last":"Carvelli","name":"Carvelli, Christain","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3377929.3389961","isbn":["9781450371278"],"pages":"71-72","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"GECCO '20: Proceedings of the 2020 Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089726267"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","modl.ai"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-03c46043-9784-4720-a144-78e3a6855258"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving HyperNetworks for Game-Playing Agents","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381315","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"An important goal in reinforcement learning is to create agents that can quickly adapt to new goals while avoiding situations that might cause damage to themselves or their environments. One way agents learn is through exploration mechanisms, which are needed to discover new policies. However, in deep reinforcement learning, exploration is normally done by injecting noise in the action space. While performing well in many domains, this setup has the inherent risk that the noisy actions performed by the agent lead to unsafe states in the environment. Here we introduce a novel approach called Meta-Learned Instinctual Networks (MLIN) that allows agents to safely learn during their lifetime while avoiding potentially hazardous states. At the core of the approach is a plastic network trained through reinforcement learning and an evolved “instinctual” network, which does not change during the agent's lifetime but can modulate the noisy output of the plastic network. We test our idea on a simple 2D navigation task with no-go zones, in which the agent has to learn to approach new targets during deployment. MLIN outperforms standard meta-trained networks and allows agents, after an evolutionary training phase, to learn to navigate to new targets without colliding with any of the no-go zones. These results suggest that meta-learning augmented with an instinctual network is a promising new approach for RL in safety-critical domains.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-385011"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary algorithms","Life long learning","Reinforcement learning","Safe reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safe reinforcement learning through meta learned instincts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85571020/MLIN_Alife_2020.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-385011","identifier":[{"id":"86000191364","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fefbb96e-cd02-4b75-a166-381a3295b91c"],"keyword":["Evolutionary algorithms","Life-long learning","Reinforcement learning","safe reinforcement learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A9ADD5E158949821EEC122DB81C2C186"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85571020/MLIN_Alife_2020.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1162/isal_a_00318","edition":"32","issn":["26931508"],"pages":"183-291","publisher":"MIT Press","series":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","status":"p","subtitle":"The 2020 Conference on Artificial Life","title":"ALIFE 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000191364"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fefbb96e-cd02-4b75-a166-381a3295b91c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Safe Reinforcement Learning through Meta-learned Instincts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-385011","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In continual learning, an agent is exposed to a changing environment, requiring it to adapt during execution time. While traditional reinforcement learning (RL) methods have shown impressive results in various domains, there has been less progress in addressing the challenge of continual learning. Current RL approaches do not al-low the agent to adapt during execution but only during a dedicated training phase. Here we study the problem of continual learning ina 2D bipedal walker domain, in which the legs of the walker grow over its lifetime, requiring the agent to adapt. The introduced approach combines neuroevolution, to determine the starting weights of a deep neural network, and a version of deep reinforcement learning that is continually running during execution time. The proof-of-concept results show that the combined approach gives abetter generalization performance when compared to evolution or reinforcement learning alone. The hybridization of reinforcement learning and evolution opens up exciting new research directions for continually learning agents that can benefit from suitable priors determined by an evolutionary process.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384174"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Continual Learning","Meta learning","Reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards continual reinforcement learning through evolutionary meta learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84798816/GECCO_POSTER_2019_Grbic_Risi_nocpyright.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384174","identifier":[{"id":"85070636226","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c6212d40-15e2-4332-b91f-3567cc5350ca"],"keyword":["Continual learning","Meta-learning","Reinforcement learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-10CA81675713F7AEDAEB03D39D22B4FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84798816/GECCO_POSTER_2019_Grbic_Risi_nocpyright.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3319619.3322044","edition":"2019","eisbn":["9781450367486"],"pages":"119-120","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Towards Continual Reinforcement Learning through Evolutionary Meta-Learning","volume":"Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070636226"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c6212d40-15e2-4332-b91f-3567cc5350ca"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Continual Reinforcement Learning through Evolutionary Meta-Learning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384174","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
